    "nsfw": false,
    "truncatedDescription": "I decided to make bread.\r\n\r\nHow hard could it be?\r\n\r\nApparently, very.\r\n\r\nWhat started as a completely normal attempt at baking bread slowly turned into an absolute disaster. Dough, flour, a declaration of war, and one deeply unfortunate loaf late...",
    "description": "I decided to make bread.\r\n\r\nHow hard could it be?\r\n\r\nApparently, very.\r\n\r\nWhat started as a completely normal attempt at baking bread slowly turned into an absolute disaster. Dough, flour, a declaration of war, and one deeply unfortunate loaf later… here we are.\r\n\r\nWelcome to the beginning of my war against bread. 🍞⚔️💥\r\n\r\nBread: 1\r\nMe: 0\r\n\r\n-------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nINGREDIENTS:\r\n\r\n2tsp dry active yeast \r\n\r\n1tbs sugar \r\n\r\n1.5c warm water \r\n\r\n3c bread flour (I used normal flour so I don't think it matters that much)\r\n\r\n2tsp salt \r\n\r\nINSTRUCTIONS:\r\n\r\nPut the yeast, sugar, and water in a bowl. Mix and cover with plastic wrap or a towel and let it rise for 5 - 10 mins, or until its foamed up. Put your flour and salt in there, mix it and cover. Let the dough rise for 2 hours and when done, start preheating  your oven to 275°C. Place your dough in a dutch oven and score. If you don't have a dutch oven you can place  your dough in a loaf pan with another on top. Place in the oven for 25 mins with the lid on, then take the lid off and let it bake for 5 minutes or until you have achieved the perfect golden crust.\r\n\r\n If you have any questions, feel free to let me know in the comments, I hope my video gave you a good chuckle, and see you in the next one. Byeeeee! ",
